      "text": "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\nGiven \n\ud835\udc50\n=\n\ud835\udf06\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n, find \n\ud835\udf06\n.\n\nChoose an answer\n\u2713\nCorrect choice selected.\n\n\u2212\n1\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n\u2212\n2\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n2\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n1\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n0\n\nCORRECT\nPreview only\nSolution:\n\nAnswer \u00b7 correct value:\n\n\u2212\n1\n\nDraw \n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n from the common origin \n\ud835\udc42\n to a point \n\ud835\udc43\n, then complete the path from \n\ud835\udc43\n to the endpoint \n\ud835\udc36\n of \n\ud835\udc50\n.\n\nThe vector \n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n points left, while \n\ud835\udc4e\n points right. Their lengths are equal, so\n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n=\n\u2212\n\ud835\udc4e\n.\nAdding the two path vectors gives\n\ud835\udc50\n\t\n=\n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc43\n\u2192\n+\n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n\n\t\n=\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n\u2212\n\ud835\udc4e\n\n\t\n=\n\u2212\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n.\nBecause \n\ud835\udc4e\n and \n\ud835\udc4f\n are nonparallel, their coefficients are unique. Comparing with \n\ud835\udc50\n=\n\ud835\udf06\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n gives \n\ud835\udf06\n=\n\u2212\n1\n. The minus sign records direction; the equal lengths give magnitude \n1\n.\n\nBack to study \u2192",
